<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Danish jobless seen lower again in April.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Danish jobless seen lower again in April.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine economists polled by Reuters forecast an average seasonally adjusted Danish unemployment rate of 7.9 percent in April compared to March's 8.0 percent.</p>
<p>The estimates were in the 7.8-8.0 percent range.</p>
<p>&quot;Danish unemployment continues its downward trend, but the pace is slackening,&quot; chief economist Joergen Birger Christensen at Den Danske Bank told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Danish national statistics office publishes its April jobless data on Thursday May 29 at 0730 gmt.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
